# 1 Why a real photon is not enough

Lesson 44 forbade a single-vertex process e→eγ on shell, and Lesson 57 forbade γ→e⁺e⁻ for the same reason: an on-shell photon has q²=0, while a pair has (p+p′)²≥4m². A static electric field is not a particle and need not lie on q²=0. In the A_0=−Ez gauge the background can transfer energy eE×distance without transferring a lightlike four-momentum. That is the opening Lesson 57 postponed.

